+
+# RQ-0124 — Closed Won / Order activated → draft invoice
+
+## Question
+
+- **Q1.** §11.2 leaves the invoice trigger open (Opportunity Closed Won or Order activation). What
+  do we build until the owner decides?
+- **Q2.** How do we know an Opportunity is won, and an Order activated, from CDC change events?
+- **Q3.** Where do the invoice lines come from — the Opportunity event carries no line items?
+- **Q4.** How do the Avro payloads encode Date and Currency fields, and how do we turn a currency
+  value into money without floating-point arithmetic?
+- **Q5.** What makes it idempotent per Opportunity/Order id, given the same event can arrive twice
+  and later edits of a won Opportunity produce further events?
+- **Q6.** Invoice date, due date, lock-date policy, warnings (PROFILE_GAP, TAX_CODE_CONFLICT) and
+  the status write-back: what does each come from?
+
+## Why it matters
+
+A second draft per Opportunity is a double invoice (and, under auto-approve, a double posting).
+A missed line under-bills. A float-parsed amount violates AGENTS.md §4.
+
+## Sources consulted
+
+| # | Source | Accessed | Kind | What it says |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| S1 | Design §4.3 (Standard invoice: "Opportunity Closed Won, Order activated, manual — lines from OpportunityLineItem / OrderItem"), §5.3 (CDC on Opportunity, OpportunityLineItem, Order, OrderItem), §5.5 field table (Opportunity + line items / Order + OrderItem are SF-owned billing sources), §11.2 "Invoice trigger default" (open) | 2026-11-09 | primary (spec) | Both triggers are in scope; default undecided; line items are their own CDC entities. |
+| S2 | RQ-0004 (Pub/Sub CDC), findings on entity selection | 2026-11-09 | prior research | Default CDC selection = Account, Contact, Opportunity, OpportunityLineItem, Product2; Order/OrderItem swap in when the tenant picks Order-based invoicing. |
+| S3 | RQ-0098 F1–F3 (master-data mapping) and `inbound/changes.ts` | 2026-11-09 | prior research / code | UPDATE bodies carry only header-named fields; commit numbers order changes of a record system-wide; across channels there is no ordering guarantee. |
+| S4 | Salesforce, *Opportunity* field reference (developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.sfFieldRef.meta/sfFieldRef/salesforce_field_reference_Opportunity.htm) and *OpportunityChangeEvent* reference (…/salesforce_field_reference_OpportunityChangeEvent.htm), via web search 2026-11-09 | 2026-11-09 | vendor docs (search summary; the docs host is not reachable from this sandbox) | `IsWon` ("Won") and `IsClosed` ("Closed") are boolean fields derived from the stage; the sample create event shows `StageName`, `IsClosed`, `IsWon`. Whether `IsWon` is listed in `changedFields` on a stage change is **not** stated. |
+| S5 | Salesforce, *ChangeEventHeader Fields* (…/change_data_capture/cdc_event_fields_header.htm) | 2026-11-09 | vendor docs (search summary) | `changedFields` lists the fields changed by an UPDATE (plus LastModifiedDate), empty for other change types; must be decoded (bitmap) in Pub/Sub API. |
+| S6 | Salesforce, *Order* and *OrderStatus* object reference (…/object_reference/sforce_api_objects_order.htm, …_orderstatus.htm), *OrderItem* reference | 2026-11-09 | vendor docs (search summary) | An Order's `StatusCode` is `Draft` or `Activated`; every `Status` picklist value belongs to one of the two; activation is an update of `Status`. OrderItem `TotalPrice` defaults to UnitPrice × Quantity. |
+| S7 | Salesforce, *Event Deserialization Considerations* (developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-deserialization-considerations.html) and *REST sobject eventSchema* example, via web search | 2026-11-09 | vendor docs (search summary) | After Avro decoding, Date and Date/Time values arrive as epoch numbers; numeric fields are typed `double` in the event schema (`"Data:Double:…"`). Avro's `date` convention is an int of days since 1970-01-01. |
+| S8 | `packages/modules/ar/src/sales-invoices.ts` (T-0040), `packages/ledger/src/period.ts` `resolvePostingDate` (T-0023), `packages/modules/products/src/profile-resolution.ts` (T-0039), `writeback/mapping.ts` (T-0067) | 2026-11-09 | code | createSalesInvoice is idempotent per (company, key); autoApproveSalesInvoice returns the draft reason; resolvePostingDate implements `reject` / `post_to_first_open_date_with_note`; the resolver throws PROFILE_GAP / TAX_CODE_CONFLICT; the write-back contract already has `invoice.drafted` and the Opportunity `invoiceStatus` / `amountInvoiced` fields. |
+
+## Findings
+
+1. **Q1 — trigger setting.** Build both behind a per-company setting `trigger_source`
+   (`opportunity` | `order`), default `opportunity`, as the card says. The setting is data with
+   history (who, why), like `ar_invoice_settings`. Recorded as a §11.2 placeholder, not a decision
+   of the open item (DL-0370).
+2. **Q2 — won / activated.** Because S4 does not guarantee that `IsWon` appears in an UPDATE's
+   changed fields, the remembered full record state (patches merged as in T-0065) is evaluated:
+   an Opportunity is won when `IsWon` is `true` **or** `StageName` is one of the company's won
+   stage names (setting, default `["Closed Won"]` — the standard won stage). An Order is activated
+   when `StatusCode` is `Activated` (S6). The trigger fires when the merged state says won or
+   activated, whichever event made it so.
+3. **Q3 — lines.** Lines come from the remembered OpportunityLineItem / OrderItem records whose
+   `OpportunityId` / `OrderId` is the source (S1, S2), stored like the T-0065 record state. Across
+   channels events are unordered (S3), so completeness is checked: the sum of the live lines'
+   `TotalPrice` must equal the header's `Amount` (Opportunity) / `TotalAmount` (Order), which
+   Salesforce rolls up from those lines. A won source with no lines or a mismatch raises a
+   **waiting** billing issue (`NO_LINES` / `LINES_INCOMPLETE`) and creates nothing; the next line
+   or header change re-evaluates it. No REST query is made (no extra API calls, no live org).
+4. **Q4 — encodings.** Date fields: int days since epoch → `YYYY-MM-DD` (UTC); a `YYYY-MM-DD`
+   string (polled snapshot) is accepted as is. Currency/number fields: an Avro `double` is turned
+   into its shortest round-trip decimal text (ECMAScript Number→String, which is exact for any
+   value with ≤ 15 significant digits) and parsed with decimal.js; a value with a non-zero digit
+   beyond the cent is refused (`INVALID_AMOUNT`), never rounded. No float arithmetic happens.
+   Documented fixture schemas follow S7; a recorded scratch-org schema replaces them later
+   (follow-up T-0160).
+5. **Q5 — idempotency.** Two layers: (a) each billing record keeps its last version
+   (commit number + sequence / SystemModstamp); a change with the same version is a duplicate,
+   counted with its key, and does nothing (design §5.6 rule 1); (b) one trigger row per
+   (company, source entity, source record Id), unique in the database, links the single invoice,
+   and the invoice's idempotency key is `sf:<Entity>:<Id18>` — a later event of a drafted source
+   only bumps a counter. Edits after drafting do not amend the draft (follow-up T-0161).
+6. **Q6 — document facts.** Invoice date = Opportunity `CloseDate` / Order `EffectiveDate`, passed
+   through `resolvePostingDate(sourceType 'ar_invoice')`: `reject` → billing issue
+   `PERIOD_LOCKED`, no draft; `post_to_first_open_date_with_note` → the first open date and the
+   policy's note as the invoice memo (SS-UC01-08). Due date = invoice date + the setting's payment
+   terms (default 14 days, as GP-001's "terms 14 days"; per-party terms are not modelled yet,
+   T-0162). Line amount = `TotalPrice` (tax-exclusive, the Salesforce price convention), product by
+   `Product2Id` → `product.salesforce_product_id`, party by `AccountId` →
+   `party.salesforce_account_id`; tax code left to the posting profile (DL-0260). Each line is
+   resolved once at draft time; any resolver refusal (PROFILE_GAP, TAX_CODE_CONFLICT, …) becomes a
+   warning stored with the trigger, and auto-approve is not attempted. Otherwise
+   `autoApproveSalesInvoice` decides. Write-back: `invoice.drafted` (status Draft) on creation and
+   `invoice.posted` (status Posted, number, total, amount invoiced) after an auto-post, through the
+   transactional outbox in the same transaction (T-0067 contract v1).
+
+## Conclusion
+
+Implement a billing-source applier beside the T-0065 master-data applier: remember
+Opportunity/OpportunityLineItem/Order/OrderItem state per record (versioned, duplicates counted),
+evaluate the source after every change, and create at most one draft per source through T-0040,
+with lock policy, warnings, auto-approve and the outbox write-back as in F6. Migration 0044 adds
+the four tenant tables (record state, trigger, issue, settings). Unverified vendor details (IsWon
+in changedFields, double/int encodings) are handled defensively and listed for a scratch-org
+recording (T-0160).
